    "body": "We have to be careful here; the spec notes that delimiters can also apply to collections, which is relevant to our security mitigations. If the brower ignores a protected collection usage it could unexpectedly expose blocklisted functionality like mouse or keyboards inputs.\n\nThis warrants further investigation to understand how different operating systems handle delimited usages at the collection level. I've never encounted a device with delimited usages so I think it's somewhat rare.\n\nTo ensure the blocklist is handled correctly, the spec should require that all usages are read and stored somewhere even if the `HIDCollection` only exposes the first delimited usage.\n\nDelimited usages for report items are not security-relevant so I think it's fine to only give the first usage for simplicity.",
